The Bard's Arsenal, a martial comedy in one act.

Hamlet, the measure of damage.
Romeo, the price of action.
Juliet, the certainty of aim.
Ophelia, the haste of the scene.
Macbeth, the shield against misfortune.
Othello, the balm that restores the wounded.

Act I: Four weapons upon the stage.

Scene I: quill thrust.
[Enter Hamlet and Romeo]
Romeo:
You are as fierce as the sum of a brave noble gentle hero and the sum of a brave noble hero and a brave hero.
Hamlet:
You are as fair as a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Juliet and Ophelia]
Ophelia:
You are as certain as the sum of a brave noble gentle fair mighty proud hero and the sum of a brave noble gentle fair hero and the sum of a brave noble gentle hero and a brave noble hero.
Juliet:
You are as swift as the sum of a brave hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Macbeth and Othello]
Othello:
You are as guarded as the difference between a hero and a hero.
Macbeth:
You are as healthy as the difference between a hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene II: tragic monologue.
[Enter Hamlet and Romeo]
Romeo:
You are as fierce as the sum of a brave noble gentle fair hero and the sum of a brave noble hero and a brave hero.
Hamlet:
You are as costly as the sum of a brave hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Juliet and Ophelia]
Ophelia:
You are as certain as the sum of a brave noble gentle fair mighty proud hero and the sum of a brave noble gentle hero and the sum of a brave noble hero and a brave hero.
Juliet:
You are as still as the difference between a hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Macbeth and Othello]
Othello:
You are as guarded as the difference between a hero and a hero.
Macbeth:
You are as healthy as the difference between a hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene III: aside parry.
[Enter Hamlet and Romeo]
Romeo:
You are as fierce as the sum of a brave noble hero and the sum of a brave hero and a hero.
Hamlet:
You are as costly as a brave hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Juliet and Ophelia]
Ophelia:
You are as certain as the sum of a brave noble gentle fair mighty proud hero and the sum of a brave noble gentle fair mighty hero and a brave noble hero.
Juliet:
You are as swift as a brave noble hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Macbeth and Othello]
Othello:
You are as guarded as the sum of a brave noble gentle hero and a brave noble hero.
Macbeth:
You are as healthy as the difference between a hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]

Scene IV: immortal verse.
[Enter Hamlet and Romeo]
Romeo:
You are as fierce as the sum of a brave noble gentle hero and a brave hero.
Hamlet:
You are as costly as the sum of a brave hero and a hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Juliet and Ophelia]
Ophelia:
You are as certain as the sum of a brave noble gentle fair mighty proud hero and the sum of a brave noble gentle fair hero and the sum of a brave noble gentle hero and a brave hero.
Juliet:
You are as swift as a brave hero.
[Exeunt]
[Enter Macbeth and Othello]
Othello:
You are as guarded as the difference between a hero and a hero.
Macbeth:
You are as healthy as the sum of a brave noble gentle hero and a brave hero.
[Exeunt]
